# Agent Architecture & Code Generation Rules

## Canonical testcase step prose

**Manual step text and expected results** for alignment with generated or hand-maintained specs live in **`src/agent/examples/sample-testcases.csv`** (per-row `Case ID`, `Test Steps`, `Expected`). Category CSVs under `src/data/<category>/` supply **runtime test data** (`testData.*`), not the full numbered step document. When analyzing a spec against its testcase, read the matching `sample-testcases.csv` row first.

When steps describe a **full BTMS precondition path** (office, agent, switch user, post automation, customer, new load), align **each segment to POMs** — use `setupOfficePreConditions` for office-only; avoid replacing the entire path with `setupDFBTestPreConditions` unless the testcase explicitly allows a bundled shortcut. Reference: `DFB-97739.spec.ts`, `DFB-97788.spec.ts`.

## 3-Agent Pipeline (LLM Disabled)

Generation is rule-based. The pipeline is:
1. **StepProcessor** (Agent 1) — classifies raw test steps into `ProcessedStep` with `PageContext` (tracks `currentPage`, `isEditMode`, `currentTab`, `currentApp`)
2. **POMMethodMatcher** (Agent 2) — matches steps to existing POM methods or proposes new ones using `AppSourceIndexer` data
3. **SpecValidator** (Agent 3) — validates generated spec against guardrails, auto-fixes violations (including NAV-001 for missing navigateToBaseUrl)

## Application Source Locators

The `AppSourceIndexer` scans cloned repos (`modetrans/mono.git`, `modetrans/dme.git`) for HTML elements. Cache lives in `src/agent/.cache/`.

### View Mode vs Edit Mode

- **Edit mode**: Form elements exist with exact `#id` — use `page.locator('#id')` with `.inputValue()` / `.fill()`
- **View mode**: Same fields render as plain text in `<td>` — use Playwright chained locators: `page.getByRole('row', { name: /Label/i }).locator('td').nth(1)` with `.textContent()`
- The `StepProcessor` tracks `isEditMode`; `POMMethodMatcher` uses it to choose the locator strategy

## MANDATORY: navigateToBaseUrl() Before Header Navigation

**Detail/form pages** (View Office Info, View Customer, Edit Load, View Carrier, Edit Office, etc.) do NOT render the main navigation header buttons (Admin, Customers, Loads, Finance, Home, etc.).

**Rule**: Call `pages.basePage.navigateToBaseUrl()` **before** `pages.basePage.hoverOverHeaderByText()` when the browser may still be on a **detail or form** surface from a prior step so the main header exists. **Do not** add `navigateToBaseUrl()` immediately after `BTMSLogin` / on the default post-login dashboard before the first header action — the landing shell already exposes the header (same pattern as `DFB-97739.spec.ts` Step 2 → office without a preceding navigate).

This is enforced at three levels:
1. **StepMappings** — all HOVER and NAVIGATION entries prepend `navigateToBaseUrl()`
2. **SpecValidator (NAV-001)** — detects and auto-fixes missing `navigateToBaseUrl()` before `hoverOverHeaderByText()`; skips when `BTMSLogin` appears within the prior `NAV_BTMS_LOGIN_LOOKBACK_LINES` (post-login precondition band; same value as PromptsConfig)
3. **PromptsConfig guardrail** — `navigateToBaseUrlBeforeHeaderNav` flags violations at generation time (same lookback logic as NAV-001)

The call is idempotent — safe even if already on the base URL. Reference specs: BT-67846, BT-74418, DFB-97739.

```typescript
// CORRECT — after login on dashboard: first header nav may omit navigate (header visible)
await pages.btmsLoginPage.BTMSLogin(userSetup.globalUser);
await pages.basePage.hoverOverHeaderByText(HEADERS.ADMIN);

// CORRECT — after office / view customer / edit load: restore shell before header nav
await pages.basePage.navigateToBaseUrl();
await pages.basePage.hoverOverHeaderByText(HEADERS.CUSTOMER);
await pages.basePage.clickSubHeaderByText(CUSTOMER_SUB_MENU.SEARCH);

// WRONG — will fail if browser is on a detail/form page without navigateToBaseUrl first
await pages.basePage.hoverOverHeaderByText(HEADERS.CUSTOMER);
```

## MANDATORY: Billing Toggle User Switch

**All test cases in the `billingtoggle` category** MUST switch to `USER_ROLES.BILLINGTOGGLE_USER` after the initial login. This is enforced at three levels:
1. **StepMappings** — BILLINGTOGGLE_USER pattern generates the correct switch code
2. **SpecValidator (CAT-BT-001)** — detects missing `USER_ROLES.BILLINGTOGGLE_USER` in billingtoggle specs and auto-fixes by injecting the switch after `BTMSLogin`
3. **PromptsConfig** — `BILLING_TOGGLE_USER_SWITCH` rule documents the requirement

```typescript
// CORRECT — billing toggle specs
await pages.btmsLoginPage.BTMSLogin(userSetup.globalUser);
await pages.homePage.clickSwitchAccountButton();
await pages.agentAccountsPage.clickOnUserNameIfVisible(USER_ROLES.BILLINGTOGGLE_USER);

// WRONG — missing user switch (will fail CAT-BT-001)
await pages.btmsLoginPage.BTMSLogin(userSetup.globalUser);
```

The constant `USER_ROLES.BILLINGTOGGLE_USER` is defined in `globalConstants.ts`. NEVER hardcode the username string directly. Reference spec: BT-74421.

## Billing toggle: View Load vs View Billing (Waiting On / finance)

When generating or editing **billingtoggle** (and similar load-finance) tests, follow the **same POM layer and order as the canonical spec** `src/tests/AIAgent/billingtoggle/BT-74454.spec.ts` (also listed first in `REFERENCE_SPECS.billingtoggle` / `ReferenceSpecAnalyzer`).

| Surface | DOM / source | POM | Read Waiting On |
|--------|----------------|-----|------------------|
| **View Load → Load tab** | `loadform.php`: **`select#fi_waiting_on`** (option values `Agent` / `Billing`, strings) | `ViewLoadPage` | `clickloadTab()`, `scrollWaitingOnIntoView()`, `getBillingIssuesWaitingOnDisplayLabel()` — assert with `PAYABLE_TOGGLE_VALUE.*` |
| **View Billing** | `billing.php`: **`#finance_issues_block`**, hidden `#fi_waiting_on` (numeric 1/2/3) + slider | `LoadBillingPage` | `scrollBillingIssuesBlockIntoView()`, `getBillingToggleValue()`, `isNotDeliveredFinalChecked()`, finance message helpers |

**Rules**

1. **After Save on Edit Load** when the testcase says **View Load** (or the app returns to View Load): validate Waiting On with **`ViewLoadPage`**, not `LoadBillingPage.getBillingToggleValue()`.
2. **After View Billing** is open: use **`LoadBillingPage`** for `#fi_waiting_on` / billing issues block.
3. **View Load from View Billing** may open a **new tab** — resolve the active `Page` via `ViewLoadPage.resolveViewLoadPageAfterBillingClick`, then use **`const vl = new PageManager(viewWorkPage)`** for all POM calls (`vl.viewLoadPage`, `vl.loadBillingPage`, etc.). Do **not** `new ViewLoadPage(...)` / `new LoadBillingPage(...)` in specs (BT-74454 Steps 6–7).
4. Billing issue **tags** (e.g. Not Deliv. Final, Price Difference) on View Load use **`ViewLoadPage`** helpers scoped to the Waiting On table — do not use `sharedPage.locator` in specs.

`PromptsConfig.REFERENCE_PATTERNS.BILLING_TOGGLE_VIEW_LOAD_VS_VIEW_BILLING` documents the same split for template/snippets.

## Test execution structure (no skipped steps / validations)

1. **Preserve testcase order** — actions and **expected** outcomes from the source sheet (e.g. CSV) appear in the same sequence in generated code.
2. **Every explicit expected** gets an **`expect` / `expect.soft`** or structured alert handling (`validateAlert` / `acceptAllDialogsDuringAction` + assertion on dialog text) — not `console.log` alone.
3. Use **nested `test.step(...)`** titles that reference **step numbers and/or expected text** (e.g. `CSV 53: …`, `Step 5 [CSV 44-48]: …`) so reports map 1:1 to the written case and reviewers can see no step was dropped.
4. Prefer **`PAYABLE_TOGGLE_VALUE`**, **`BILLING_ISSUE_TAGS`**, **`LOAD_STATUS`**, **`ALERT_PATTERNS`** over hardcoded strings in assertions.

## Assertion Values

Never hardcode expected values in assertions. Use:
- `INVOICE_PROCESS.OFFICE`, `AUTOPAY_STATUS.ENABLED`, `PAYABLE_TOGGLE_VALUE.AGENT`, `FINANCE_MESSAGES.LOAD_NOT_INVOICED` from `globalConstants.ts`
- `testData.*` from CSV for dynamic values (rates, amounts, names)

## POM Method JSDoc

Every new POM method must include: `@author AI Agent`, `@created YYYY-MM-DD`, `@param` (if applicable), `@returns` (if applicable), and locator source reference.

## Report grid locators (Billing Queue / Load Search)

DataTables report grids (`report_sizzle.phtml`) share `#example_wrapper table#example`. **Never** use page-wide `table.table`, `table.report-table`, `table` + `.first()`, `table tbody tr`, or `thead th` — they race hydration and leak rows/headers from clone tables.

```typescript
// CORRECT — scoped grid (BillingQueuePage, AllLoadsSearchPage)
this.resultsTable_LOC = this.page.locator("#example_wrapper table#example");
this.tableHeaders_LOC = this.resultsTable_LOC.locator("thead > tr > th");
this.resultsDataRows_LOC = this.resultsTable_LOC.locator("tbody > tr[role='row']"); // Billing Queue
// Load Search: resultsTable.locator("tbody > tr.dnd-moved")
```

`PromptsConfig.GENERATION_RULES.REPORT_GRID_LOCATORS` and `REFERENCE_PATTERNS.REPORT_GRID_LOCATORS`.

## Report column labels (string constants, not RegExp)

Column lookup uses **exact UI label strings** from `BILLING_QUEUE_COLUMNS` / `LOAD_SEARCH_COLUMNS`. POM `getColumnIndex(string[])` / `getColumnCellValues(string[])` normalizes whitespace and compares case-insensitively.

```typescript
// CORRECT
await pages.billingQueuePage.getColumnCellValues([BILLING_QUEUE_COLUMNS.INITIAL_TOGGLE_DATE]);
await pages.billingQueuePage.getColumnCellValues([
  BILLING_QUEUE_COLUMNS.AGENT_TOGGLE_DATE,
  BILLING_QUEUE_COLUMNS.CURRENT_TOGGLE_DATE,
]);

// WRONG — SpecValidator SAN-026/027/028 + guardrail noRegExpReportColumnLabels
getColumnCellValues([new RegExp(BILLING_QUEUE_COLUMNS.INITIAL_TOGGLE_DATE, "i")]);
```

Reference specs: `BT-116909.spec.ts`, `BT-116910.spec.ts`. Snippet: `REFERENCE_PATTERNS.BILLING_QUEUE_COLUMN_LOOKUP`.

## REGEX_PATTERNS module (`src/utils/regexPatterns.ts`)

Date/datetime parsing and billing-block label extraction use `REGEX_PATTERNS` — **never** inline regex in POM parse helpers.

| Key | Use |
|-----|-----|
| `DATE.US_REPORT_DATETIME` | Billing Queue report cell dates |
| `DATE.US_FILTER_DATE` | Datepicker filter inputs |
| `BILLING_TOGGLE.INITIAL_TOGGLE_DATE_LABEL` | `#finance_issues_block` text |
| `TEXT.WHITESPACE_RUNS` | Header/cell normalization |

`PromptsConfig.GENERATION_RULES.REGEX_PATTERNS_MODULE` · `REFERENCE_PATTERNS.REGEX_PATTERNS_USAGE`.

## View History User — exact SYSTEM assertion

System-generated audit entries write the fixed literal `"SYSTEM"`. Use exact equality with `VIEW_HISTORY_USER.SYSTEM` — not `toMatch(/system/i)`.

```typescript
expect(row.user).toBe(VIEW_HISTORY_USER.SYSTEM);
```

Enforced: `SAN-029`, guardrail `noFuzzyViewHistoryUserAssertion`. Reference: `BT-97807.spec.ts`.

## Chained widget locators

Declare container id once; chain children off it (single source of truth, scoped to parent).

```typescript
this.statusMultiselectContainer_LOC = this.page.locator("#search_status_magic");
this.statusMultiselectTrigger_LOC = this.statusMultiselectContainer_LOC.locator(".ms-trigger");
```

`GENERATION_RULES.CHAINED_COMPONENT_LOCATORS` · `REFERENCE_PATTERNS.CHAINED_WIDGET_LOCATORS`.
